<title>UK: Steel products freighter broken in two at Busan.</title>
<headline>Steel products freighter broken in two at Busan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thailand-flagged freighter Jutha Jessica, laden with some 2,000 tonnes of steel products, ran aground and broke in two at southern harbour Busan, South Korea, on January 1, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence said.</p>
<p>The 13,579 dwt vessel had been lying anchored awaiting a cargo loading berth, but dragged its anchor due to strong winds and ran aground on rocks. It is totally submerged.</p>
<p>Some bunker fuel was reported leaking from the vessel.</p>
<p>Of the 29 crew members who were on board, 24 were rescued, two were found dead and three are still missing.</p>
